# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# ────────────── Dependencies ──────────────
node_modules/
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# ────────────── Testing ──────────────
coverage/

# NOTE: `scripts/` used to be ignored wholesale. That was wrong: it holds hand-written,
# source-controlled verification harnesses, and package.json references `test:e2e:smoke` as
# an npm script. With the directory ignored that script resolved to a file which existed
# only on one machine and was missing from every clone.

# ────────────── Next.js Build Artifacts ──────────────
.next/
out/
build/

# ────────────── Environment Configs ──────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local

# ────────────── Debug Logs ──────────────
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ────────────── TypeScript ──────────────
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ────────────── Deployment (e.g. Vercel) ──────────────
.vercel/

# ────────────── Miscellaneous ──────────────
.DS_Store
*.pem

# `CHANGELOG.md` is intentionally untracked: it is a local release log, not shared project
# documentation. It stays on disk and remains recoverable from history at any commit
# (`git show <rev>:CHANGELOG.md`). Re-track with `git add -f CHANGELOG.md` if that changes.
CHANGELOG.md

*storybook.log
storybook-static
.velite/